text><line x1=\"8\" x2=\"610\" y1=\"213.9\" y2=\"213.9\" stroke=\"#6B6152\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 4\" class=\"\"/><text x=\"616\" y=\"217.9\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#6B6152\"><tspan font-weight=\"700\">$933.38</tspan> 61.8% retrace</text><line x1=\"8\" x2=\"610\" y1=\"242.0\" y2=\"242.0\" stroke=\"#2F6E4A\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 4\" class=\"\"/><text x=\"616\" y=\"246.0\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#2F6E4A\"><tspan font-weight=\"700\">$879.27</tspan> 50% retrace</text><line x1=\"8\" x2=\"610\" y1=\"270.2\" y2=\"270.2\" stroke=\"#6B6152\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 4\" class=\"\"/><text x=\"616\" y=\"274.2\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#6B6152\"><tspan font-weight=\"700\">$825.17</tspan> 38.2% retrace</text><line x1=\"8\" x2=\"610\" y1=\"303.1\" y2=\"303.1\" stroke=\"#1B8FA8\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" class=\"\"/><text x=\"616\" y=\"307.1\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#1B8FA8\"><tspan font-weight=\"700\">$761.89</tspan> 200-day avg</text><line x1=\"8\" x2=\"610\" y1=\"361.4\" y2=\"361.4\" stroke=\"#A63A2E\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" class=\"\"/><text x=\"616\" y=\"365.4\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#A63A2E\"><tspan font-weight=\"700\">$650.00</tspan> Nov low</text><circle cx=\"515.1\" cy=\"277.4\" r=\"3.5\" fill=\"#C9A84C\" stroke=\"#20242C\" stroke-width=\"1\"/></svg></figure>\n<p>These lines are mine, not yours. You have not sent Fib levels for MU.</p>\n<ul><li><strong>Trend:</strong> mixed. Close $811.30 (Nov 11), above the 200-day ($761.89) but below the 20-day ($849.67) and the 50-day ($950.43). It only got back over the 200-day on Nov 11.</li><li><strong>Momentum:</strong> RSI 45.1. Below the midline, not washed out.</li><li><strong>Ceiling:</strong> $825.17, the 38.2% retracement of the drop from $1,108.55 (Sep 25) to $650.00 (Nov 5). The Nov 11 high was $827.58 and the close came back under it. Then the 20-day at $849.67, $879.27 (50%) and $933.38 (61.8%). The 52-week high is $1,254.61 (Jun 25).</li><li><strong>Floor:</strong> the 200-day at $761.89, then the $650.00 low. The 52-week low is $192.37 (Nov 21, 2025).</li><li><strong>Your tested edge:</strong> does not apply. Price and the 50-day are above the 200-day, so the uptrend half holds, but RSI is 45.1, not under 40. It did apply on Nov 2 and Nov 4 (RSI 37.4 and 35.4); from Nov 5 to Nov 10 price was under the 200-day.</li><li><strong>Scorecard:</strong> no open or watching play on MU.</li><li><strong>Verdict:</strong> the chart supports neither side yet. A close above $825.17 leans up and opens $879.27. A close back below $761.89 leans down and points at $650.00. That is a disagreement with management, in part: they described the strongest outlook in the group, and the stock is 35% under its June high and has recovered barely a third of its latest drop. The market is pricing the worry above, not the guidance.</li></ul>\n<h3 id=\"what-would-change-this-read\">What would change this read</h3>\n<ul><li>The next report (date not found; the quarter ends around Nov 30). Watch gross margin against 86.25% and what they say about pricing after Q1.</li><li>Price data: a quarter where contract DRAM prices stop rising, or a second sign that AI chips will carry less memory each.</li><li>Nvidia on Nov 17 and the Fed on Dec 8–9. Both bear on whether the customers keep spending at this pace.</li></ul>\n<h3 id=\"confidence-and-sources\">Confidence and sources</h3>\n<p>Solid: results, guidance, contracts and balance sheet (company release, prepared remarks, 10-K). Medium: question-and-answer detail and the TrendForce price figures, which are forecasts and differ between the two reports. Thin: lead independent director, vote results, legal proceedings (10-K read in part only), the next report date, and the 121% figure, which is from a headline.</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"https://finviz.com/news/397277/micron-technology-inc-reports-record-fiscal-fourth-quarter-and-full-year-2026-results\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">FQ4 release copy</a> · <a href=\"